          "title": "Senior Frontend Developer | React.Js Developer",
          "description": "As a Senior Frontend Developer at Bitcot, I’ve led the development of dynamic, scalable, and performance-driven web applications across various domains including healthcare, e-commerce, and nonprofit fundraising. My work spans both greenfield projects and legacy system enhancements, with a strong focus on user experience, maintainable code, and seamless cross-platform functionality. I specialize in building robust applications using React.js and Next.js, with a deep understanding of SSR, SEO optimization, modular architecture, and state management using Redux and React Hook Form. I've architected and delivered end-to-end solutions for real-time platforms, integrated third-party SDKs (like 100ms for video conferencing), and optimized UI performance through virtualization, lazy loading, and code splitting. Key contributions include: Delivering responsive, accessible, and localized UIs using i18n, WCAG standards, and Tailwind CSS Building and maintaining reusable UI libraries to standardize form controls and design components across products Integrating APIs (REST, Firebase, AWS, etc.) and implementing secure role-based access and region-specific privacy logic Enhancing a medical image analysis tool (Next.js + Cornerstone.js) with custom DICOM rendering, SVG-based landmark tools, and analytical measurement workflows Supporting e-commerce platforms by working across React and JSP codebases, including admin panel development, user management, policy management, and React-AcceptJS payment integrations Collaborating closely in Agile teams with product managers, designers, and backend engineers to ensure efficient delivery Throughout my role, I’ve consistently focused on writing clean, maintainable code, contributing to code reviews, and mentoring junior developers where needed. My goal is always to bridge design and functionality with precision, scalability, and user empathy.",
