          "title": "Senior Product Manager",
          "description": "Branded experiences: Technical Product manager for the Activity lifecycle Platform, Intelligent Communications Platform, and Server Presentation Framework platform that is built on the principle of Server Driven UI\n\nActivity Lifecycle Platform\nA highly scalable and multi-tenant platform that enables you to store, search, and manage activities of PayPal customers. An activity is any user action that is of significance for a customer's engagement with PayPal. So we are a platform that provides the foundational backend for the consumer and merchant facing domains to help them deliver powerful end-user experiences\nI own the Ingestion, Search, Scheduler, and Fanout capabilities that have sub-second latencies. The platform currently serves 5B search requests and 7B ingestions monthly.\n\nIntelligent Communications Platform\nPlatform that manages product related communication through channels such as Push Notifications, Email, SMS, Notification Center, Badging (in-app/out-of-app).\n\nServer Presentation Framework\nPlatform that works on the principal of Server Driven UI and hence, leverages the server to build the user interfaces of their client apps.\nClients call the server to fetch the templates which contains the UI components and the data required to be rendered on the screen. Templates are then passed to SPF SDK which returns the user interface to the client.\nThis opens up new possibilities and addresses some fundamental challenges with native mobile app development or web development. \nSPF serves ~100M monthly requests for templates with sub-second latency from various User experience teams and roughly 50% experiences on the PayPal super app are powered through SPF.\n\nAll these platforms are leveraged for several Digital Wallet programs under the Super App initiative @PayPal",
